timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:55:35Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Correct, vs the more common anustup chhandah", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:56:08Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Although the popular version of the first line is 7 syllables long", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:58:32Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "That’s the invocation correct?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:58:44Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Yeah", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:58:45Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "The verse proper starts from tatsaviturvarenyam", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:58:48Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Which is 8", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:59:34Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "https://youtu.be/YXfRsS8MzX4?si=2x7jEsXBNCnwzjaL", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T20:59:45Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Question stolen from this video", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:02:03Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "The part about difficulty is v true", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:02:53Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Plus i think w/o a proper guru in the disciplic succession line it’s hard to get proper essence and even pronunciations", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:04:03Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Gatekeeping using weird notions of adhikara rooted in caste etc is also hurting their preservation, although i do support certain vedapatshalas were caste and gender are not bars", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:04:53Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Academic study also seems limited, mostly they seem to focus on dharmashastras and upanishads", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:08:40Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "This video made me realize another factor: the people who wrote the vedas lived in a pastoral society with very different values, customs, hopes, and fears compared to the settled agricultural and industrial societies that their descendants built in the subcontinent. The people who wrote the itihasas and puranas lived in settled agricultural societies with values more similar to ours.", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:08:53Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Definitely", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:09:29Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "The rigvedic ppls were definitely tribal, pastoral. Martial", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:09:56Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Hence the connection to steppe migrants and ‘aryan migration theory’ but i dont buy all of it", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:10:07Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Because the IVC was a settled civ", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:10:27Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Recent excavations are pointing to waves of migrations in both directions", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-03T21:11:07Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Indra is the archetypal leader of a pastoralist tribe always on the move. Rama and Krishna are archetypes of leadership in a settled agricultural society.", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]